#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:2
msgid "Release Schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:5
msgid "Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:7
msgid ""
"Syncthing follows the `Semantic Versioning <http://semver.org/>`__ scheme of "
"versioning. Each release has a three part version number: *major*.\\ *minor*."
"\\ *patch*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:11
msgid ""
"A new *major* version is released when there are incompatible API or "
"protocol changes, a new *minor* version is released when there are new "
"features but compatibility with older releases is retained, and a new "
"*patch* version is released when there are bug fixes (compatibility with "
"older releases always retained)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:17
msgid ""
"While still in pre-release mode, i.e. versions 0.\\ *x*, breaking changes "
"are made in minor releases rather than major. Version 0.7.3 should be able "
"to talk to version 0.7.52, but will probably not understand version 0.8.0. "
"This also means that if you don't like 0.7.52, you can safely downgrade to "
"0.7.3 again and keep your configuration, index caches, etc. However 0.8.0 "
"might have a different format for those things so a downgrade to 0.7.x might "
"be trickier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:26
msgid "Patch Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:28
msgid ""
"A new patch release is made each Sunday, if there have been changes "
"committed since the last release. Serious bugs, such as would crash the "
"client or corrupt data, cause an immediate (out of schedule) patch release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:34
msgid "Minor Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:36
msgid ""
"Minor releases are made when new functionality is ready for release. This "
"happen approximately once every few weeks, with the pace slowing as the 1.0 "
"release nears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:41
msgid "Major Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-schedule.rst:43
msgid ""
"A new major release is a rare event. At the time of writing this has not yet "
"happened and is foreseen to happen only once in the foreseeable future - the "
"1.0 release."
msgstr ""
